1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:03,732
Coronary artery disease is the
world's leading cause of death.

2
00:00:03,942 --> 00:00:08,406
A risk score can tell a doctor how likely
disease is, but not where it is, and

3
00:00:08,426 --> 00:00:11,124
finding that out still
takes an invasive angiogram.

4
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:14,561
This is AngioLens, our project for Track A.

5
00:00:14,784 --> 00:00:19,427
It is a virtual angiogram. From routine
clinical data it predicts coronary artery

6
00:00:19,447 --> 00:00:24,523
disease and stenosis in each of the three
main arteries, explains every number

7
00:00:24,543 --> 00:00:28,455
exactly, and maps the result
onto a real 3D heart.

8
00:00:29,463 --> 00:00:31,860
Every session opens with a safety notice.

9
00:00:32,131 --> 00:00:37,209
Behind it is the dashboard, showing patient
ninety-nine from the real Z-Alizadeh

10
00:00:37,323 --> 00:00:40,046
Sani cohort of three
hundred and three patients.

11
00:00:40,304 --> 00:00:45,164
The green tag matters. This patient is
replayed by the cross-validation model that

12
00:00:45,184 --> 00:00:49,721
never saw them in training, so what you
see is honest, out-of-sample behaviour.

13
00:00:49,968 --> 00:00:54,575
The model estimates a seventy-four percent
probability of coronary disease and

14
00:00:54,595 --> 00:00:59,299
points to the LAD, at sixty-five percent,
while confidently ruling out the

15
00:00:59,319 --> 00:01:04,275
circumflex. The real angiogram
agrees: single-vessel LAD

16
00:01:04,295 --> 00:01:05,082
disease.

17
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:09,246
The heart is real anatomy from BodyParts3D.

18
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:14,833
The LAD, circumflex and right coronary
trees are selected by their anatomical

19
00:01:14,853 --> 00:01:18,681
identifiers and sit on a
corrected epicardial surface.

20
00:01:18,927 --> 00:01:24,100
Each artery is coloured by its predicted
probability, and contrast boluses flow from

21
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:29,534
the ostium toward the apex. In high-risk
vessels the flow slows and flickers,

22
00:01:29,661 --> 00:01:31,986
like delayed filling on an angiogram.

23
00:01:32,209 --> 00:01:34,258
Let me click the LAD to isolate it.

24
00:01:34,504 --> 00:01:39,496
The inspector shows its probability, its
conformal confidence and the factors that

25
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:43,801
localise disease there, led by
the reduced ejection fraction.

26
00:01:44,783 --> 00:01:49,571
The tinted muscle is the territory each
artery supplies, linked to the American

27
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:52,745
Heart Association
seventeen-segment bull's-eye.

28
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:56,255
Hover a segment and its
artery lights up in 3D.

29
00:01:56,490 --> 00:02:01,700
Click any point on the heart muscle, and
AngioLens shows which arteries perfuse it.

30
00:02:01,946 --> 00:02:06,267
The heart even beats at the patient's
recorded pulse, fifty beats per minute here,

31
00:02:06,562 --> 00:02:10,833
next to a schematic ECG built from their
actual findings, including the T-wave

32
00:02:10,853 --> 00:02:11,459
inversion.

33
00:02:12,459 --> 00:02:15,938
Why these numbers?
AngioLens is hierarchical.

34
00:02:16,185 --> 00:02:18,871
Stage one asks whether
there is coronary disease.

35
00:02:19,105 --> 00:02:22,092
Stage two asks which artery, given disease.

36
00:02:22,327 --> 00:02:27,379
The vessel probability is the product, so
it can never exceed the overall risk, a

37
00:02:27,399 --> 00:02:31,683
rule that independent per-vessel models
break for about one patient in five.

38
00:02:31,930 --> 00:02:37,260
Each stage blends a sparse logistic regression
with gradient boosting in log-odds,

39
00:02:37,483 --> 00:02:42,619
then calibrates it. Because every step
is affine, the SHAP values add up

40
00:02:42,639 --> 00:02:44,880
exactly to the probability on screen.

41
00:02:45,175 --> 00:02:50,011
For this patient, typical chest pain and
T-wave inversion push the risk up, while

42
00:02:50,031 --> 00:02:52,260
the absence of hypertension pulls it down.

43
00:02:52,507 --> 00:02:57,549
Switching to the LAD stage, the low ejection
fraction is what points to this artery.

44
00:02:57,795 --> 00:03:02,427
Below, every measurement appears against
its reference range, with its exact

45
00:03:02,447 --> 00:03:03,306
contribution.

46
00:03:04,292 --> 00:03:06,558
New patients can be entered in three ways.

47
00:03:06,804 --> 00:03:11,796
Pick a preset, edit any of the
fifty-five fields, or import a JSON or

48
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:16,389
CSV file, even a raw row from
the original UCI spreadsheet.

49
00:03:16,624 --> 00:03:20,452
This one is a seventy-two year
old man with three-vessel disease.

50
00:03:20,686 --> 00:03:25,077
Every change re-predicts in about forty
milliseconds, so the arteries, the

51
00:03:25,097 --> 00:03:28,084
territories and the
explanations update live.

52
00:03:28,331 --> 00:03:31,389
Watch the heart as I remove
his typical chest pain.

53
00:03:32,392 --> 00:03:35,655
The What-if tab probes the
model, here on patient five.

54
00:03:35,890 --> 00:03:38,936
Counterfactual probes show
what drives an estimate.

55
00:03:39,159 --> 00:03:41,941
Risk-factor targets reveal
something important.

56
00:03:42,164 --> 00:03:47,468
Setting LDL to seventy slightly raises
the modelled risk, as it does for

57
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:49,225
most patients in this cohort.

58
00:03:49,459 --> 00:03:54,391
That is confounding by treatment: LDL is
no higher in diseased patients, because

59
00:03:54,411 --> 00:03:59,706
many are already on statins. So
AngioLens flags these as associations,

60
00:03:59,796 --> 00:04:05,293
not treatment effects. Sensitivity
curves show how all four risks move with

61
00:04:05,313 --> 00:04:06,496
any single feature.

62
00:04:07,492 --> 00:04:09,710
We also show where the model fails.

63
00:04:09,956 --> 00:04:14,744
The Missed filter lists patients it got
wrong out-of-fold, like patient twenty: a

64
00:04:14,764 --> 00:04:19,289
true coronary case with no typical
chest pain, rated at just seven percent.

65
00:04:19,523 --> 00:04:24,612
Localising disease from routine data is
genuinely hard, so conformal prediction

66
00:04:24,632 --> 00:04:28,878
marks uncertain vessel calls as
indeterminate instead of painting a falsely

67
00:04:28,898 --> 00:04:32,810
confident heart, and its ninety
percent coverage holds out-of-sample.

68
00:04:33,045 --> 00:04:38,494
When the evidence is strong, as in patient
fifteen with three-vessel disease, every

69
00:04:38,514 --> 00:04:40,455
artery lights up with a confident call.

70
00:04:41,471 --> 00:04:46,763
The copilot turns all of this into language,
for clinicians or patients, in English

71
00:04:46,783 --> 00:04:49,253
or Hindi, by text or by voice.

72
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,873
The language model never predicts anything.

73
00:04:52,108 --> 00:04:57,160
It rephrases a fact sheet produced by
the model, and every number it writes is

74
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:59,049
automatically checked against that sheet.

75
00:04:59,319 --> 00:05:04,251
Here, every one is verified. Questions that
the model output cannot answer, such as

76
00:05:04,271 --> 00:05:09,456
drug dosing, are declined. And
one click exports a one-page PDF

77
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:10,070
report.

78
00:05:11,131 --> 00:05:16,678
Finally, the model card. Everything is
validated with ten-times repeated, nested,

79
00:05:16,804 --> 00:05:21,892
five-fold cross-validation, so
hyper-parameters, calibration, thresholds and

80
00:05:21,912 --> 00:05:24,430
conformal sets never touch the test fold.

81
00:05:24,665 --> 00:05:29,921
Overall coronary disease
reaches an AUC of 0.93, the LAD

82
00:05:29,941 --> 00:05:35,402
0.84, and the circumflex and right
coronary artery about 0.71 to

83
00:05:35,422 --> 00:05:40,835
0.74. Against four strong
baselines, AngioLens matches

84
00:05:40,855 --> 00:05:45,919
the best discrimination, has the best or
tied-best Brier score, and is the only

85
00:05:45,939 --> 00:05:48,553
model that is always anatomically coherent.

86
00:05:48,787 --> 00:05:53,709
Decision-curve analysis shows clinical
net benefit across referral thresholds.

87
00:05:54,671 --> 00:05:59,278
Under the hood, a single feature registry
drives training, validation and the

88
00:05:59,298 --> 00:06:04,543
interface. A FastAPI backend returns
predictions with exact SHAP for all four

89
00:06:04,563 --> 00:06:09,771
stages in about forty milliseconds, and
a React Three Fiber front end with custom

90
00:06:09,791 --> 00:06:13,847
shaders runs at sixty frames per
second on integrated laptop graphics.

91
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:19,472
Twenty automated tests guard against leakage
and check exact additivity, coherence

92
00:06:19,599 --> 00:06:25,109
and reproducibility. The whole pipeline,
from training to the 3D asset, the report

93
00:06:25,296 --> 00:06:28,883
and even this video, is
scripted and reproducible.

94
00:06:29,895 --> 00:06:35,417
AngioLens is a decision-support and
educational prototype, not a diagnosis.

95
00:06:35,652 --> 00:06:40,656
It is trained on a single centre, uses
generic anatomy, and shows associations

96
00:06:40,676 --> 00:06:45,127
rather than causes. But it shows how a
prediction can become a picture that a

97
00:06:45,147 --> 00:06:49,216
clinician can question. Thank
you, from Random Forest Rangers.
